@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# P3-T9: Ask Bun asks Opus again in a fresh conversation
+
+- **Status:** built and verified locally on `p3/t9-ask-escalation`, from `origin/claude/p1a-vault-core`. Not pushed. Under R87 this receipt is its own file; `premium-progress.md` is not edited. Under R100 whole suites are CI's (the full workers suite, the full render suite and its sections, the exports and the database suites). No HTTP route, app entry, config or catalogue section changed, so `typecheck:routes` and `export:web` are not in the local gate.
+- **Delivers:** D28 as H7. Haiku 5.5 answers first, its whole conversation under 25 s of the route's 55 s (H3). When its answer fails the grounding check, it declines, or it ends without an answer (the turn limit, a cut-short or empty answer, or a turn the deadline never let start), Opus 5.5 is asked again in a fresh conversation: the person's question alone, as Haiku first saw it, with the same system and tools and the rest of the deadline. An outage never escalates. When neither model's words can be shown, the plain figures answer (Opus's, else Haiku's), or Bun's could-not-find line. A question counts one use, which goes back when no model's words are shown and the last call failed with an outage (H5, R116). Each figure carries its record count and what it counts over (H14), and the phone needs both. The P3-T8 reviews' carries ride along: a model date that is no calendar date no longer crashes a read, `choices` lives once, and the slip's tokens count only what the API reported as counts.
+- **Files:**
+  - New:
+    - `apps/edge/src/v1/ai/ask.ts`: `ASK_MAX_TURNS`, `AskOutcome`, `AskDeps`, `runAskConversation`, `askWithEscalation`.
+    - `apps/edge/test/workers/ask-escalation.test.ts` (13 cases: the plan's 10, the P3-T7 reviews' PR3 as two rows and PK).
+    - `apps/edge/test/ask-deadline.test.ts` (Node, 12 cases: the plan's slow-conversation case and how one conversation ends).
+    - `docs/implementation/receipts/P3-T9.md` (this receipt).
+  - Modified (shared):
+    - `packages/contracts/src/v1/ai.ts`: `AiFigureScope`; `AiFigure` gains `count` and `scope`; `AiAskResult`'s comment. `packages/contracts/src/index.ts`: exports `AiFigureScope`.
+    - `apps/edge/src/v1/ai/service.ts`: Ask Bun asks through `askWithEscalation` and gives the use back after every answer through `giveBack` (which refunds only when no model's words are shown and the last call failed with an outage); parse uses `draftChoices`; the header names each route's model (the P3-T8 second review's n2).
+    - `apps/edge/src/v1/ai/uses.ts`: R116 in `shouldRefund`, and the P3-T7 second review's n1 wording.
+    - `apps/edge/src/vault/ai.ts`: each tool's figures carry `count` and `scope`.
+    - `apps/edge/src/server/ai/drafts.ts`: `isRealDate` refuses a date that is no calendar date instead of throwing; `draftChoices` (the one copy of what a model may choose from).
+    - `apps/edge/src/v1/ai/slip-read.ts`: `draftChoices`; a draft the sanitizer cannot read leaves the answer unusable; `tokens` count only counts.
+    - `apps/edge/test/workers/ai.test.ts`, `ai-uses.test.ts`, `slip-read.test.ts`, `apps/edge/test/ai-grounding.test.ts`: the cases below.
+    - `apps/app/src/spend/v1/ai/aiResources.ts`: `isAiAskResult` needs each figure's `count` and `scope`. `aiResources.test.ts`: one case, and the ask row's figure.
+    - Type-only fixtures: `apps/app/src/dev/catalogue/companion/companionSections.tsx`, `apps/app/src/screens/redesign/ai/AskBunScreen.render.test.tsx` and the figure in `ai-grounding.test.ts`.
+    - `docs/implementation/receipts/P3-T8.md`: its risk note's second refund-after-billing path, and R116's change to its "unchanged" note.
+- **RED to GREEN** (typed stubs: `ask.ts` holds today's Ask Bun in the new shape, with no Opus; `vault/ai.ts` answers `count` and `scope` null; `drafts.ts` has `draftChoices` but no date guard; `uses.ts`, `slip-read.ts` and `aiResources.ts` at base; the root, app and edge typechecks pass at RED):
+  - `apps/app` `src/spend/v1/ai/aiResources.test.ts` (Node): RED `tests 4, pass 1, fail 3`, GREEN `tests 4, pass 4`.
+  - `apps/edge` `test/ask-deadline.test.ts` and `test/ai-grounding.test.ts` (Node): RED `Tests  6 failed | 40 passed (46)`, GREEN `Tests  46 passed (46)`.
+  - Workers, under the heavy lock, `ask-escalation`, `ai-uses`, `ai.test`, `ai-routing` and `slip-read`: RED `Tests  26 failed | 100 passed (126)`, GREEN `Tests  126 passed (126)`.
+  - Every RED failure is an `AssertionError`. Passing at RED by design (pins of what must stay true): a Haiku outage never reaches Opus and is logged by name; the P3-T7 reviews' Ask Bun refund pins (PR3 at 529 and 500, PK); the moved conversation's grounded, ungrounded, five-turn, outage, rejected and tool-step rows; and the P3-T8 reviews' slip pins on code that was already right (an Opus outage after any unusable Haiku answer, an Opus answer with no draft, the media type, the archived choices, a bare answer, the trace's offset).
+- **Mutation check:** `mutants.py`, 79 of 79 killed, every failing case of every kill an `AssertionError`; each file restored byte for byte. The plan's five: P1 (Haiku's turns replayed to Opus), P2 (escalate on a 429), P3 (a second use for Opus), P4 (Haiku given the parent deadline) and P5 (paused whenever no figures exist). The conversations K1 to K29; the service S1 to S6 (S6 is the P3-T7 second review's M9); R116 U1 to U4; the figures V1 to V10; the phone A1 to A12; the P3-T8 carries D1 to D3, R1 to R6 and T1 to T5 (the reviews' O1, O2, O3, O6 and MJ).
+- **Fast local gate (R100):**
+  - `npm run typecheck` (contracts changed), `npm run typecheck:app`, `npm run typecheck:edge`: passed.
+  - The focused files above: RED to GREEN as listed.
+  - The render files on the AI fakes (`TellBunSheet`, `AskBunScreen`, `BunNote`, `CompanionSettings`, `CashbackCard`, `AnalyticsUpkeep`, `AmountStep`, `AddTray`, `walletHarness`, `WalletRecap`, `WalletAiSettings`, `AiConsent`) and the four routes tests (`SpendRoutes`, `account/AccountRoutes`, `insights/InsightsRoutes`, `planning/PlanningRoutes`): passed.
+  - `test:edge`, `test:app`, `test:unit`: passed. `build:edge`: passed. `git diff --check`: clean.
+- **CI (R100):** the full `test:edge:workers`, the full render suite and sections 1 to 3 (the catalogue's whole-catalogue files render `catalogueAi`), `export:web` and the iOS export, `test:edge:db` and `test:db` (Docker is stopped locally), `test:ops`.
+- **Deviations:** the brief's planner rulings P1 to P16 (`.claude/controller/briefs/P3-T9.md`), as accepted by the controller. In short: the conversations log their own failed calls by class name; a vault refusal at a tool step is the route's answer and a failed step ends that conversation as an outage; R116 lives in `shouldRefund` for every route; `escalated` is true whenever the question went to Opus; the category name is `string | null`; `fakeAiResources.ts` needs no change; the P3-T8 reviews' must-carry items and pins ride along.
+- **Client minimum (P6C):** the phone's Ask Bun validator now needs each figure's `count` and `scope`, and an older app refuses the new answer (exact keys). Any release carrying P3-T9 needs a client minimum of at least `AI_MIN_CLIENT_VERSION` (`0.2.0`), with the server's minimum versions raised in the same release (the followups' release rule for P6C-T6 applies).
+- **Risks:**
+  - An escalated question makes calls to both models for one use (D28); the question counts once, as the spec says.
+  - A question no model could be asked in time (only when the vault steps leave under 2 s of the 55) answers Bun's could-not-find line, with its use given back, as the plan's rules read (a turn that cannot start is `no_answer`).
+  - Refunds after billed calls stay uncapped (the owner's refund-caps item): an Ask Bun outage after an ungrounded Haiku answer gives the use back after a billed Haiku call, as Review Focus 3 asks.
+- **Notes for later tasks:**
+  - **P3-T10:** both conversations' calls are in the one trace, Opus's marked `escalated: true`; a turn the deadline never let start is recorded `sent: false` (no `$ai_generation`). Ask Bun's failed calls still log `ai_fallback` by class name; a decline or an ungrounded answer that escalates logs nothing.
+  - **P3-T20 (Ask Bun in the Bun Wallet look):** `count` reads "41 records" and `scope` offers the records behind a figure; a place's total has a count and no scope, a budget line neither. `escalated` can be true on a plain-figures answer.
+  - **P4-T4 (import mode):** `shouldRefund` now carries R116 for the slip too: a per-slip deadline must leave Opus at least 2 s after Haiku's 20 s cap, or a read whose Opus call never starts spends its use. `draftChoices` is the one place the choices are built.
+  - **P5-T18e (currency):** `ask.ts` is where the currency reaches Ask Bun's figures and words; they stay in baht until then (B7).
